HELPMENU {
[1;37mQuick start[0m
 1. Set 2 (news server) and 3 (port); 6 and 7 if the server wants a
    login.  Port 119 is plain NNTP; for TLS use 563 and set 4 to TLS.
 2. Press G and link each newsgroup to a forum.  Create the forum
    first, with the usual forum tools.
 3. Set 1 to YES.  Press C to check right away; the status line and
    the Audit Trail show how it went.

 Messages users write in a linked forum are posted to the newsgroup,
 and the newsgroup's articles appear in the forum.  Type a setting's
 number to change it; ? at any prompt explains it, and H with a
 number (e.g. H 12) explains a setting from here.
} T Quick-start help


HELPGRP {
[1;37mNewsgroup links[0m
 Each link joins one newsgroup to one forum.  Import copies the
 group's articles into the forum; Export posts what users write in
 the forum to the group.  Several newsgroups may share one forum:
 export then posts to all of them at once, as one cross-posted article.
 The State column shows "new" until the first check, then the number
 of the next article to read, or PROBLEM: open the link to see why.
} T Help on the newsgroup screens


